IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cbca-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cb4-common`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part XV, s 189: BORROWING POWERS AND
-- EXTRAORDINARY SALE, LEASE OR EXCHANGE.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice Canada consolidation
-- current to 2026-09-30; not verified against the official text.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE IS. Subsections (1) and (2) let the directors borrow, guarantee and give security
-- without asking the shareholders, unless the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement
-- say otherwise, and delegate that power. Subsections (3) to (9) require the shareholders' approval of a
-- sale, lease or exchange of all or substantially all the corporation's property outside the ordinary
-- course of business.
-- "A unanimous shareholder agreement" is defined in section 146 (piece cb3); whether the articles, by-laws
-- or such an agreement "otherwise provide" is a plain input.

§§ `s 189(1) and (2) Borrowing powers`

-- src:2335 | 189 (1) Unless the articles or by-laws of or a unanimous shareholder agreement relating to a corporation otherwise provide, the directors of a corporation may, without authorization of the shareholders,
-- src:2336 | (a) borrow money on the credit of the corporation;
-- src:2337 | (b) issue, reissue, sell, pledge or hypothecate debt obligations of the corporation;
-- src:2338 | (c) give a guarantee on behalf of the corporation to secure performance of an obligation of any person; and
-- src:2339 | (d) mortgage, hypothecate, pledge or otherwise create a security interest in all or any property of the corporation, owned or subsequently acquired, to secure any obligation of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 189(1) (src:2335-2339)
DECLARE `Kind of financing power under s 189(1)` IS ONE OF
    `to borrow money on the credit of the corporation (s 189(1)(a))`
    `to issue, reissue, sell, pledge or hypothecate debt obligations of the corporation (s 189(1)(b))`
    `to give a guarantee on behalf of the corporation to secure performance of an obligation of any person (s 189(1)(c))`
    `to mortgage, hypothecate, pledge or otherwise create a security interest in all or any property of the corporation to secure any obligation of the corporation (s 189(1)(d))`
    `a power that s 189(1) does not list`

@ref CBCA s 189(1) (src:2335-2339)
GIVEN power IS A `Kind of financing power under s 189(1)`
      `the articles otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the by-laws otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors may exercise the power without the shareholders' authorization within s 189(1)` MEANS
        (CONSIDER power
         WHEN `to borrow money on the credit of the corporation (s 189(1)(a))` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `to issue, reissue, sell, pledge or hypothecate debt obligations of the corporation (s 189(1)(b))` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `to give a guarantee on behalf of the corporation to secure performance of an obligation of any person (s 189(1)(c))` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `to mortgage, hypothecate, pledge or otherwise create a security interest in all or any property of the corporation to secure any obligation of the corporation (s 189(1)(d))` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND (NOT `the articles otherwise provide`)
    AND (NOT `the by-laws otherwise provide`)
    AND (NOT `a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provides`)

-- (2): delegation "notwithstanding subsection 115(3) and paragraph 121(a)" (pieces cb2). The notwithstanding
-- clause removes those two provisions as obstacles, so they are not inputs.
DECLARE `Person to whom the borrowing powers are delegated (s 189(2))` IS ONE OF
    `a director delegated the borrowing powers (s 189(2))`
    `a committee of directors`
    `an officer delegated the borrowing powers (s 189(2))`
    `a person who is neither a director, a committee of directors nor an officer (s 189(2))`

-- src:2340 | Delegation of borrowing powers
-- src:2341 | (2) Notwithstanding subsection 115(3) and paragraph 121(a), unless the articles or by-laws of or a unanimous shareholder agreement relating to a corporation otherwise provide, the directors may, by resolution, delegate the powers referred to in subsection (1) to a director, a committee of directors or an officer.
@ref CBCA s 189(2) (src:2341)
GIVEN delegate IS A `Person to whom the borrowing powers are delegated (s 189(2))`
      `the directors delegate by resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the by-laws otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors may delegate the powers in subsection 189(1) within s 189(2)` MEANS
        (CONSIDER delegate
         WHEN `a director delegated the borrowing powers (s 189(2))` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a committee of directors` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `an officer delegated the borrowing powers (s 189(2))` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND `the directors delegate by resolution`
    AND (NOT `the articles otherwise provide`)
    AND (NOT `the by-laws otherwise provide`)
    AND (NOT `a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provides`)

§§ `s 189(3) to (9) Extraordinary sale, lease or exchange`

-- "All or substantially all" is a judgment the Act leaves to the facts; it is an input.
-- src:2342 | Extraordinary sale, lease or exchange
-- src:2343 | (3) A sale, lease or exchange of all or substantially all the property of a corporation other than in the ordinary course of business of the corporation requires the approval of the shareholders in accordance with subsections (4) to (8).
@ref CBCA s 189(3) (src:2343)
GIVEN `the sale, lease or exchange is of all or substantially all the property of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is other than in the ordinary course of business of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the sale, lease or exchange needs the approval of the shareholders within s 189(3)` MEANS
        `the sale, lease or exchange is of all or substantially all the property of the corporation`
    AND `it is other than in the ordinary course of business of the corporation`

-- src:2344 | Notice of meeting
-- src:2345 | (4) A notice of a meeting of shareholders complying with section 135 shall be sent in accordance with that section to each shareholder and shall
-- src:2346 | (a) include or be accompanied by a copy or summary of the agreement of sale, lease or exchange; and
-- src:2347 | (b) state that a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares in accordance with section 190, but failure to make that statement does not invalidate a sale, lease or exchange referred to in subsection (3).
@ref CBCA s 189(4) (src:2345-2347)
GIVEN -- out of range: section 135 (piece cb3)
      `the notice complies with section 135` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is sent to each shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice includes or is accompanied by a copy or summary of the agreement of sale, lease or exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares in accordance with section 190` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the notice of the meeting complies within s 189(4)` MEANS
        `the notice complies with section 135`
    AND `the notice is sent to each shareholder`
    AND `the notice includes or is accompanied by a copy or summary of the agreement of sale, lease or exchange`
    AND (    (NOT `a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares in accordance with section 190`)
         OR  `the notice states that a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares`)

@ref CBCA s 189(4)(b) (src:2347)
GIVEN `the omission of the dissent statement was the only failure of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Effect on validity of leaving out the dissent statement`
`the effect on the sale, lease or exchange of leaving out the dissent statement within s 189(4)(b)` MEANS
    `the effect of leaving out the dissent statement` `the omission of the dissent statement was the only failure of the notice`

-- src:2348 | Shareholder approval
-- src:2349 | (5) At the meeting referred to in subsection (4), the shareholders may authorize the sale, lease or exchange and may fix or authorize the directors to fix any of the terms and conditions thereof.
@ref CBCA s 189(5) (src:2349)
GIVEN `the meeting is the meeting referred to in subsection 189(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shareholders may authorize the sale, lease or exchange and fix or authorize the directors to fix its terms within s 189(5)` MEANS
    `the meeting is the meeting referred to in subsection 189(4)`

-- src:2350 | Right to vote
-- src:2351 | (6) Each share of the corporation carries the right to vote in respect of a sale, lease or exchange referred to in subsection (3) whether or not it otherwise carries the right to vote.
@ref CBCA s 189(6) (src:2351)
GIVEN `the share otherwise carries the right to vote` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the share carries the right to vote on the sale, lease or exchange within s 189(6)` MEANS TRUE

-- (7): "only if" -- a class or series votes separately only if it is affected in a manner different from
-- the shares of another class or series. This differs from section 176: no list of changes.
-- src:2352 | Class vote
-- src:2353 | (7) The holders of shares of a class or series of shares of the corporation are entitled to vote separately as a class or series in respect of a sale, lease or exchange referred to in subsection (3) only if such class or series is affected by the sale, lease or exchange in a manner different from the shares of another class or series.
@ref CBCA s 189(7) (src:2353)
GIVEN `the class or series is affected by the sale, lease or exchange in a manner different from the shares of another class or series` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the holders of a class or series are entitled to vote separately on the sale, lease or exchange within s 189(7)` MEANS
    `the class or series is affected by the sale, lease or exchange in a manner different from the shares of another class or series`

-- (8): adopted when the holders of each class or series "entitled to vote thereon" have approved by special
-- resolution. Read, as in sections 176(6) and 183(5), as the special resolution of the shareholders who
-- voted AND of each class or series entitled to vote separately under (7) (fork F1).
-- src:2354 | Shareholder approval
-- src:2355 | (8) A sale, lease or exchange referred to in subsection (3) is adopted when the holders of each class or series entitled to vote thereon have approved of the sale, lease or exchange by a special resolution.
@ref CBCA s 189(8) (src:2355)
GIVEN tally IS A `Vote tally`
      `every class or series entitled to vote separately has approved by special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the sale, lease or exchange is adopted within s 189(8)` MEANS
        `special resolution within s 2(1)` tally
    AND `every class or series entitled to vote separately has approved by special resolution`

-- (9): "subject to the rights of third parties". The directors' power to abandon exists, but the
-- abandonment cannot defeat a third party's right; it is encoded as "no right of a third party is
-- defeated" (a judgment of the facts).
-- src:2356 | Termination
-- src:2357 | (9) The directors of a corporation may, if authorized by the shareholders approving a proposed sale, lease or exchange, and subject to the rights of third parties, abandon the sale, lease or exchange without further approval of the shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 189(9) (src:2357)
GIVEN `the shareholders approving the sale, lease or exchange authorized the directors to abandon it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `abandoning it would defeat a right of a third party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors may abandon the sale, lease or exchange without further approval of the shareholders within s 189(9)` MEANS
        `the shareholders approving the sale, lease or exchange authorized the directors to abandon it`
    AND (NOT `abandoning it would defeat a right of a third party`)
